\id 2JN - American Standard Version (Byzantine Text with Apocrypha)
\h 2 John
\toc1 The Second Epistle of John
\toc2 2 John
\toc3 2 Jn.
\mt2 THE SECOND EPISTLE OF
\mt1 JOHN
\c 1
\p
\v 1 The elder unto the elect lady and her children, whom I love in truth; and not I only, but also all they that know the truth;
\v 2 for the truth’s sake which abideth in us, and it shall be with us forever:
\v 3 Grace, mercy, peace shall be with us, from God the Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, in truth and love.
\b
\p
\v 4 I rejoice greatly that I have found \add certain\add* of thy children walking in truth, even as we received commandment from the Father.
\v 5 And now I beseech thee, lady, not as though writing to thee a new commandment, but that which we had from the beginning, that we love one another.
\v 6 And this is love, that we should walk after his commandments. This is the commandment, even as ye heard from the beginning, that ye should walk in it.
\v 7 For many deceivers are entered into the world, \add even\add* they that confess not that Jesus Christ cometh in the flesh. This is the deceiver and the antichrist.
\v 8 Look to yourselves, that we lose not the things which we have wrought, but that we receive a full reward.
\v 9 Whosoever transgresseth and abideth not in the teaching of Christ, hath not God: he that abideth in the teaching of Christ, the same hath both the Father and the Son.
\v 10 If anyone cometh unto you, and bringeth not this teaching, receive him not into \add your\add* house, and give him no greeting:
\v 11 for he that giveth him greeting partaketh in his evil works.
\b
\p
\v 12 Having many things to write unto you, I would not \add write them\add* with paper and ink: but I hope to come unto you, and to speak face to face, that our joy may be made full.
\v 13 The children of thine elect sister salute thee. Amen.
